  Citation: Williams CJ, Headd JJ, Moriarty NW, Prisant MG, Videau LL, Deis LN,
  Verma V, Keedy DA, Hintze BJ, Chen VB, Jain S, Lewis SM, Arendall WB,
  Snoeyink J, Adams PD, Lovell SC, Richardson JS, Richardson DC (2018).
  MolProbity: More and better reference data for improved all-atom structure
  validation. Protein Science, 27(1), 293-315. https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.3330
  What MolBioCraft derived from it: MolBioCraft does not ship the grids. It
  ships six 10-degree Ramachandran region maps derived from them (general, Gly,
  trans-Pro, cis-Pro, pre-Pro and Ile/Val), in
  crates/molbiocraft-protein/src/backbone.rs. Each 2-degree grid node is
  classed with MolProbity's cutoffs, as coded in cctbx ramalyze.py: favoured at
  a value of at least 0.02; otherwise allowed at least 0.0005 (general), 0.0020
  (cis-Pro) or 0.0010 (the other classes); otherwise outlier. Each 10-degree
  cell then takes the median class of its 25 nodes.
  scripts/outside-data/derive_ramachandran_maps.py regenerates the maps from the
  grids. The maps are a coarse approximation of MolProbity's Ramachandran
  categories, not MolProbity's classifier. Their use does not imply endorsement
  by the Richardson Lab or Duke University.
